  <string name="whatThisIs">What this is</string>
  <string name="whatCountsAsAMistake">What counts as a mistake here?</string>
  <string name="whatCountsAsAMistakeAnswer">A move where the computer evaluation swung against you, and the computer has a better move to show. It is the same selection as "Learn from your mistakes" on the analysis board, over every analysed game instead of one.</string>
  <string name="howIsThisDifferentFromPuzzles">How is this different from puzzles?</string>
  <string name="howIsThisDifferentFromPuzzlesAnswer">Puzzles come from other people's games and have a clean solution. These are your own positions, and you already got them wrong once. Nothing here is rated.</string>
  <string name="whyAreMyRecentGamesMissing">Why are my recent games missing?</string>
  <string name="whyAreMyRecentGamesMissingAnswer">Games from the last month are left out by default: you probably still remember the move. Use the controls at the top to include them.</string>
  <string name="whyCantISeeWhichGame">Why is the link to the game only there afterwards?</string>
  <string name="whyCantISeeWhichGameAnswer">The link opens the game at that move, where the computer analysis is already shown. So it waits until you have answered.</string>

